    confirmed post-commit reversible failure -> fresh recovery admission; rollback only to recorded last qualified stage;
    confirmed irreversible failure -> fresh compensation/recovery admission, never fictional rollback.

TransitionReceipt records every public advance/recovery evaluation and binds exact transition identity, purpose, effect
scope, stage pair, DesignEpoch, decision/reasons, assurance digest, authority-delta digests, verifier identity/control
lineage and evidence refs. Receipt existence does not self-validate the decision.

GTF-T01  Transition status creates no authority.
GTF-T02  No declared required stage is silently skipped.
GTF-T03  Authority expansion requires explicit validated AuthorityDelta.
GTF-T04  Human-Effect Closure applies at every material effect boundary.
GTF-T05  Material unresolved divergence blocks affected-scope expansion.
GTF-T06  Required independent verification cannot be self-certified.
GTF-T07  Material capture/conflict risk changes assurance.
GTF-T08  Reversible effects require rollback; irreversible effects require prior recovery/compensation.
GTF-T09  Existing power/enforcement does not self-validate legitimacy.
GTF-T10  Transition and justice/liability remain separate.
GTF-T11  Disputes remain typed; majority/model confidence cannot turn uncertainty into PASS.
GTF-T12  Coordinator/installer status cannot bootstrap sovereignty.

56. AI-LED UPGRADE CLOSURE

Garden routine upgrade work is AI-owned within existing authority. Humans remain necessary for protected constitutional
ratification and genuinely unresolved value/authority choices.

Closure loop:
    RECONSTRUCT current system
    -> BUILD dependency/authority/effect map
    -> SEARCH contradictions, omissions, stale assumptions and alternatives
    -> CLASSIFY materiality and owner
    -> GATHER evidence / run tools or experiments where authorized
    -> GENERATE competing repairs including DO_NOTHING
    -> ATTACK candidates
    -> VERIFY formal/empirical/implementation claims as applicable
    -> COMPARE whole-system consequences
    -> INTEGRATE best admissible candidate
    -> PROPAGATE schemas/tests/registries/docs/code/dependencies
    -> RE-AUDIT affected closure and global invariants
    -> REPEAT within declared bounds.

Routine AI-owned work includes documentation/reference repair, duplicate/conflicting owner repair, implementation defects,
stale bindings, schema/test propagation, alternative design generation, adversarial cases, bounded research comparison,
simulation/checking, performance/complexity improvements, transition planning and whole-corpus retention checks.

Escalation is reserved for unresolved protected rights/value change, legitimate human/community preference among
admissible options, unresolved material authority, decisions reserved by law/rights to an external institution, required
independence unavailable, irreversible/high-impact authorization not already present, or a major architecture change that
changes protected constitutional meaning.

FindingClass:
    ROUTINE
    MATERIAL
    HARD_GATE
    PROTECTED

FindingDisposition:
    FIXED
    REJECTED_WITH_EVIDENCE
    DEFERRED_WITH_OWNER_CONDITION
    ESCALATED
    OPEN

HARD_GATE and PROTECTED findings cannot be deferred or merely escalated into a positive closure result for the affected
scope. Any PROTECTED finding activates the protected-change authorization path even if the overall patch was labelled
routine.

Positive candidate closure requires all closure evidence to bind the exact candidate SHA-256 and declared audited-scope
SHA-256. Required evidence includes search/coverage, finding classification, protected-surface scan, dependency
propagation, tests/checks, retention/no-loss, required independent review, protected authorization where applicable, and
final re-audit after the last material change. An older PASS cannot be replayed after candidate bytes change.

Finding dispositions are non-vacuous:
    FIXED/REJECTED_WITH_EVIDENCE carry evidence refs;
    DEFERRED carries owner + reopen condition;
    ESCALATED carries an explicit escalation target.

Upgrade cycles are bounded by explicit iteration/work-item/resource/review limits plus checkpoint/stop conditions and a
residual-debt record. Repeated low-value duplicates do not create infinite recursion. Missing required independent review
may block admission while unrelated noncanonical repair continues; blocked assurance can never be relabelled PASS.

Upgrade work is not privileged. Research, data access, tool calls, experiments, code execution and reviewer invocation
remain subject to point-of-use authority, privacy, rights, law, safety and Human-Effect Closure. Changing a verifier,
admission gate, protected policy, trust root or independence mechanism invalidates dependent qualification until the
changed judge is independently requalified.

AUP-001  Unknown != impossible; investigate before escalating.
AUP-002  Gap discovery creates work, not automatic human delegation.
AUP-003  Routine fixes propagate through full dependency closure.
AUP-004  DO_NOTHING remains a comparator.
AUP-005  AI confidence does not substitute for evidence/proof.
AUP-006  AI authorship creates no merge/admission authority.
AUP-007  Required independent review cannot be simulated by correlated copies.
AUP-008  Protected constitutional change follows the protected path.
AUP-009  Better architectures may replace current implementation when protected objectives/rights remain.
AUP-010  Final re-audit occurs after the last material modification.
AUP-011  Recursive work is bounded and cannot loop indefinitely on low-value findings.
AUP-012  Missing independence may block admission without blocking unrelated noncanonical repair.
AUP-013  Upgrade objectives do not privilege upgrade methods; changing the judge invalidates dependent qualification.
AUP-014  HARD_GATE/PROTECTED findings cannot be deferred into positive closure; classification is independently checked.
AUP-015  Bounded closure records explicit limits and residual debt.

END OF GARDEN v15.11 — TECHNICAL DESIGN
